    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear priority on leveraging platoon advantages against favorable matchups. Our strongest play is **Kyle Tucker** (74.599), whose high base projection is bolstered by a massive 19% bump due to the soft matchup against Gasser. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.663) is in an elite spot batting second, where his dynamic platoon advantage against Holmes provides a significant boost, making him a cornerstone of today\u2019s production. **Sam Antonacci** also ranks as an essential start (67.675); he benefits from both the leadoff spot and a 5% wind-out factor, further validated by his strong 0.397 xwOBA. While **Andy Pages** (68.071) faces the same soft target as **Kyle Tucker**, his placement in the cleanup spot provides a slightly lower but still highly efficient floor for run production.\n\nStrategic decision-making was largely dictated by the high-caliber arm of Skenes, who suppresses **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.734) significantly despite his underlying talent. This matchup reality is why **Nolan Schanuel** (41.646) remained on the bench; while his projection is stable, he lacked the explosive platoon or park factors required to displace our current starters. We are also managing significant availability issues: **Gunnar Henderson** is out due to a rainout, and we remain without **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Coby Mayo**, **Brayan Rocchio**, and **Gage Workman**, all of whom are currently dealing with IL designations or unavailability. \n\nFinally, remain cautious regarding **Liam Hicks** (47.846) and **Jackson Merrill** (56.210). **Liam Hicks** faces a reasonably tough test against Peralta, limiting his ceiling, while **Jackson Merrill** faces a downward adjustment for both park factors and an elite catcher matchup risk that may stifle his efficiency. We are strictly monitoring weather reports, though no major impacts are projected beyond the confirmed postponement of **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s game. Focus remains on capitalizing on the favorable SP_xERA marks for our core hitters to sustain our 5x5 category standing.",
